menu "eBPF"

config KFEAT_EBPF
    bool "Enable eBPF execution engine"
    default n
    help
      Enable the in-kernel eBPF interpreter (crate `kbpf`).

      Provides a minimal BPF virtual machine that can execute eBPF
      bytecode programs and dispatch to host-registered helper
      functions following the Linux eBPF helper ABI
      (`fn(r1, r2, r3, r4, r5) -> r0`, all `u64`).

      The execution engine is being built up incrementally. The BPF
      verifier, the standard Linux helper-function set, BPF maps,
      ELF/relocation handling, tracepoint / kprobe attachment glue,
      and the `bpf(2)` syscall surface are not yet implemented;
      enabling this option only links the interpreter into the
      kernel build.

      Disable for production builds until the eBPF stack is
      feature-complete. When in doubt, say N.

endmenu
